      <version name="3.1" author="Victor Vieira (OvictorVieira)" time="2026-08-29T15:38:17Z">
        <source file="Reaset.lua" type="script" main="main">https://raw.githubusercontent.com/OvictorVieira/ReaSet/82325faab0991a2b1178de34a22e7db5f349467e/Reaset.lua</source>
        <source file="ReaSet.html">https://raw.githubusercontent.com/OvictorVieira/ReaSet/82325faab0991a2b1178de34a22e7db5f349467e/ReaSet.html</source>
        <source file="Sortable.min.js">https://raw.githubusercontent.com/OvictorVieira/ReaSet/82325faab0991a2b1178de34a22e7db5f349467e/Sortable.min.js</source>
        <changelog><![CDATA[
ReaSet v3.1: stage-reliability epic. Deterministic transport, single-Director
arbitration, Controller role, active-setlist sync across devices, visual
playback blocks, PT-BR localization, and a real-device stage test matrix.

Fixes from the first stage run: a big setlist push never reached REAPER
(bulk publishes now bypass the batched wwr_req URL), a nil-track exception
that aborted the shared-setlist write, the pt-BR "AO VIVO" tab wrapping onto
two lines, and the drawer's last section sitting under the mobile browser
toolbar.
        ]]></changelog>
      </version>
      <version name="3.2" author="Victor Vieira (OvictorVieira)" time="2026-08-29T16:00:52Z">
        <source file="Reaset.lua" type="script" main="main">https://raw.githubusercontent.com/OvictorVieira/ReaSet/0a90f845349b5b22b0d3d5a19f57b6bdc3fbeb04/Reaset.lua</source>
        <source file="ReaSet.html">https://raw.githubusercontent.com/OvictorVieira/ReaSet/0a90f845349b5b22b0d3d5a19f57b6bdc3fbeb04/ReaSet.html</source>
        <source file="Sortable.min.js">https://raw.githubusercontent.com/OvictorVieira/ReaSet/0a90f845349b5b22b0d3d5a19f57b6bdc3fbeb04/Sortable.min.js</source>
        <changelog><![CDATA[
ReaSet v3.2: imported setlists were erased by the next disk reload.
importSetlists() only touched memory and localStorage; the project library
on disk is the source of truth, so the next _librarySyncWithProject() (fired
on every dropdown open, changeSetlist and boot) silently replaced the import
with the old disk contents and "Default" reappeared selected. Import now
enqueues deletes for the names it drops and upserts for every incoming name,
and arms the disk-refresh guard so writes still in flight are not undone.
        ]]></changelog>
      </version>
      <version name="3.3" author="Victor Vieira (OvictorVieira)" time="2026-08-29T17:21:41Z">
        <source file="Reaset.lua" type="script" main="main">https://raw.githubusercontent.com/OvictorVieira/ReaSet/faa2dc9f9b0c7235915909da299cd9366a0ca07e/Reaset.lua</source>
        <source file="ReaSet.html">https://raw.githubusercontent.com/OvictorVieira/ReaSet/faa2dc9f9b0c7235915909da299cd9366a0ca07e/ReaSet.html</source>
        <source file="Sortable.min.js">https://raw.githubusercontent.com/OvictorVieira/ReaSet/faa2dc9f9b0c7235915909da299cd9366a0ca07e/Sortable.min.js</source>
        <changelog><![CDATA[
ReaSet v3.3: edit mode reworked around the whole project on one screen.
The row button toggles a song's active state in place (x deactivates, +
reactivates, nothing ever vanishes); actives always group above the grey
rows; an explicit add arrives active. LOOP is performance control now:
the Controller arms and disarms it directly, and it works on a stopped
transport via the selected song. Mobile: the transport bar tracks the
visual viewport (no more floating above Chrome's collapsed toolbar) and
the pt-BR "AO VIVO" tab stays on one line.
        ]]></changelog>
      </version>
